.TH "InitAtExit" "3" "2026\-09\-29" "TheCRatTime" "AtExit reference"
.SH NAME
\fBInitAtExit\fR \- init AtExitHeader struct.\&
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fB#include\fR <\fBatexit.h\fR>
.PP
\fBAtExitHeader* InitAtExit(int\fR \fIsize\fB);\fR
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is initial function for AtExitHeader, that used by all functions in \fBatexit_do\fR(3).\&
.PP
\fIsize\fR
.RS 4
Size of maximal nodes (maximal AtExit functions).\&
.RE
.PP
.SH RETURN VALUE
Return value is AtExitHeader* if good and \fBNULL\fR if error.\&
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
#include <atexit.h>

int main(void) {
  AtExitHeader* atexit_h = InitAtExit(0)
  /* If set 0, sets default value */
  if (atexit_h == NULL) {
    /* Error handle */
  }

  /* ... */
  return 0;
}
.fi
.PP
.SH AUTHORS
Project and man-page: TheCRatTime
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBSetAtExit\fR(3), \fBAtExitHeader\fR(3type)
